CAT = "accafaStatements"; SEG = "FST"
def m(v): return "${:,.0f}".format(v)
Q = [
("Under IFRS 18, income and expenses in the statement of profit or loss are classified into categories that include:",
 "Operating, investing and financing", ["Trading, capital and revenue", "Current, non-current and equity", "Direct, indirect and overhead"],
 "IFRS 18 uses five categories: operating, investing, financing, income taxes and discontinued operations. Their subtotals include operating profit."),
("Which subtotal must be presented in the statement of profit or loss under IFRS 18?",
 "Operating profit", ["Earnings before depreciation", "Gross margin percentage", "Cash from operations"],
 "IFRS 18 requires operating profit, profit before financing and income taxes, and profit. Gross profit is common but not required, and EBITDA is a performance measure."),
("For a retailer, interest expense on a bank loan is presented in which IFRS 18 category?",
 "Financing", ["Operating", "Investing", "Income taxes"],
 "Expenses from liabilities that only raise finance, such as bank loans, go in the financing category, below operating profit and profit before financing and income taxes."),
("Under IFRS 18, an investor's share of the profit of an associate is presented in the:",
 "Investing category", ["Operating category", "Financing category", "Other comprehensive income"],
 "IFRS 18 places income and expenses from equity-accounted investments in the investing category, outside operating profit."),
("A retailer reports revenue $820,000, cost of sales $497,000, distribution costs $61,000, administrative expenses $88,000, interest on a bank deposit $4,000 and interest on a bank loan $12,000. Its operating profit is:",
 m(820000 - 497000 - 61000 - 88000), [m(820000 - 497000 - 61000 - 88000 + 4000), m(820000 - 497000 - 61000 - 88000 + 4000 - 12000), m(820000 - 497000)],
 "Operating profit = $820,000 - $497,000 - $61,000 - $88,000 = $174,000. Deposit interest is investing and loan interest is financing, so both fall below operating profit."),
("A company reports revenue $615,000, cost of sales $362,000, operating expenses $141,000, dividends from an equity investment $6,500 and interest on loan notes $9,800. Profit before financing and income taxes is:",
 m(615000 - 362000 - 141000 + 6500), [m(615000 - 362000 - 141000), m(615000 - 362000 - 141000 + 6500 - 9800), m(615000 - 362000)],
 "Operating profit is $112,000. Adding the investing income gives profit before financing and income taxes of $118,500. Loan note interest is financing and comes after it."),
("Last year's income tax was estimated at $42,000 but was settled at $45,500. This year's estimate is $51,000. The income tax expense for this year is:",
 m(51000 + 3500), [m(51000 - 3500), m(51000), m(51000 + 45500)],
 "The $3,500 under-provision from last year is added to this year's charge: $51,000 + $3,500 = $54,500."),
("This year's income tax is estimated at $38,600. Last year's liability of $33,000 was settled for $31,200. The income tax liability in this year's statement of financial position is:",
 m(38600), [m(38600 - 1800), m(38600 + 1800), m(33000)],
 "The liability is this year's estimate, $38,600. The $1,800 over-provision only reduces this year's tax expense."),
("A bank loan repayable in equal yearly instalments over five years is presented as:",
 "Split between current and non-current", ["Wholly a non-current liability", "Wholly a current liability", "A deduction from equity"],
 "The instalment due within 12 months is a current liability and the rest is non-current."),
("Profit for the year, less dividends, increases which item in the statement of financial position?",
 "Retained earnings", ["Share premium", "Revaluation surplus", "Share capital"],
 "Profit belongs to the shareholders and builds up in retained earnings; dividends are paid out of it. This links the statement of profit or loss to the statement of financial position."),
("The main purpose of the notes to the financial statements is to:",
 "Give detail not shown in the main statements", ["Replace the statement of cash flows", "Record transactions in the ledger", "Set out the auditor's opinion"],
 "Notes explain accounting policies and break down figures, such as non-current asset movements, provisions and inventories, to help users understand the statements."),
("Which event after the reporting period is an adjusting event?",
 "Insolvency of a year-end customer", ["A fire that destroys inventory", "A large share issue", "A fall in exchange rates"],
 "A customer's insolvency after the year end gives evidence that the receivable was impaired at the reporting date. The others are conditions that arose afterwards."),
("A material non-adjusting event after the reporting period should be:",
 "Disclosed in the notes", ["Adjusted for in the statements", "Ignored until next year", "Recognised as a provision"],
 "IAS 10 requires the nature of the event and an estimate of its financial effect to be disclosed, so users are not misled, but the figures are not changed."),
("Inventory with a cost of $9,000 at the year end is sold after the year end for net proceeds of $6,500. This is:",
 "Adjusting: write down by $2,500", ["Non-adjusting: disclose only", "Adjusting: write down by $6,500", "Non-adjusting: no disclosure"],
 "The sale is evidence of the inventory's net realisable value at the year end, so inventory is written down by $2,500, from $9,000 to $6,500."),
("Under IAS 7 as amended by IFRS 18, the indirect method of calculating operating cash flows starts from:",
 "Operating profit", ["Profit for the year", "Profit before income taxes", "Revenue less cost of sales"],
 "IFRS 18 amended IAS 7 so that the indirect method reconciles from operating profit, the subtotal now required in the statement of profit or loss."),
("Operating profit is $96,000. Depreciation is $21,500 and there is a $1,800 loss on disposal. Inventories rose by $7,400, receivables fell by $3,900 and payables fell by $2,600. Cash from operating activities before income taxes is:",
 m(96000 + 21500 + 1800 - 7400 + 3900 - 2600), [m(96000 + 21500 + 1800 + 7400 - 3900 + 2600), m(96000 + 21500 - 7400 + 3900 - 2600), m(96000 + 21500 - 1800 - 7400 + 3900 - 2600)],
 "Add back depreciation and the loss, deduct the rise in inventories and the fall in payables, and add the fall in receivables: $96,000 + $21,500 + $1,800 - $7,400 + $3,900 - $2,600 = $113,200."),
("Under IAS 7 as amended by IFRS 18, a manufacturer classifies interest paid on its borrowings as cash flows from:",
 "Financing activities", ["Operating activities", "Investing activities", "Operating or financing, by choice"],
 "For an entity without a specified main business activity such as banking, the amendments remove the old choice: interest paid is financing."),
("Under IAS 7 as amended by IFRS 18, a retailer classifies dividends it receives from investments as cash flows from:",
 "Investing activities", ["Operating activities", "Financing activities", "Operating or investing, by choice"],
 "The amendments require interest and dividends received to be investing cash flows for entities without a specified main business activity."),
("Property, plant and equipment had a carrying amount of $410,000 at the start of the year and $468,000 at the end. Depreciation was $52,000 and assets with a carrying amount of $17,000 were sold. There were no revaluations. Cash paid for new assets was:",
 m(468000 + 52000 + 17000 - 410000), [m(468000 - 410000), m(468000 - 410000 + 52000 - 17000), m(468000 + 52000 - 410000)],
 "Opening $410,000 - depreciation $52,000 - disposals $17,000 + additions = closing $468,000, so additions = $127,000."),
("The income tax liability was $24,300 at the start of the year and $27,100 at the end. The tax charge in profit or loss was $29,800. Tax paid in the year was:",
 m(24300 + 29800 - 27100), [m(29800), m(29800 + 27100 - 24300), m(24300)],
 "Tax paid = opening liability + charge - closing liability = $24,300 + $29,800 - $27,100 = $27,000."),
("A benefit to users of a statement of cash flows is that:",
 "Cash is harder to manipulate than profit", ["It shows the profit for the year", "It replaces the income statement", "It shows assets at fair value"],
 "Profit depends on estimates such as depreciation and accruals, while cash flows are more objective and show whether the business can pay its way."),
("Which transaction reduces cash but has no effect on profit?",
 "Repaying a bank loan", ["Depreciating machinery", "Writing off an irrecoverable debt", "Accruing unpaid wages"],
 "Repaying a loan reduces cash and a liability equally, with no income or expense. The other three reduce profit with no cash leaving."),
("Sales were $260,000 at a gross profit margin of 30%. Opening inventory was $21,000 and purchases $186,000. Closing inventory is:",
 m(21000 + 186000 - 260000 * 0.70), [m(21000 + 186000 - 260000 / 1.30), m(186000 - 260000 * 0.70), m(21000)],
 "Cost of sales is 70% of sales, $182,000. Closing inventory = $21,000 + $186,000 - $182,000 = $25,000. Treating 30% as a mark-up on cost gives $7,000."),
("Opening inventory was $31,500 and purchases $146,000. Sales were $180,000 at a mark-up of 25% on cost. A fire destroyed most of the inventory; the rest was valued at $6,200. The cost of inventory lost was:",
 m(31500 + 146000 - 180000 / 1.25 - 6200), [m(31500 + 146000 - 180000 * 0.75 - 6200), m(31500 + 146000 - 180000 / 1.25), m(31500 + 146000 - 180000 / 1.25 - 2 * 6200)],
 "Cost of sales = $180,000 / 1.25 = $144,000. Inventory that should be on hand is $31,500 + $146,000 - $144,000 = $33,500, less $6,200 left, so $27,300 was lost."),
("Receivables were $14,600 at the start of the year and $17,250 at the end. Cash from customers was $92,400, discounts allowed $1,100 and irrecoverable debts written off $650. Credit sales for the year were:",
 m(17250 + 92400 + 1100 + 650 - 14600), [m(17250 + 92400 - 14600), m(17250 + 92400 + 1100 - 14600), m(14600 + 92400 + 1100 + 650 - 17250)],
 "Credit sales = closing receivables + cash + discounts + write-offs - opening receivables = $17,250 + $92,400 + $1,100 + $650 - $14,600 = $96,800."),
("A trader's cash takings were $64,300. She paid suppliers $41,800 in cash and banked $15,000. Cash in hand rose from $350 to $500. Her cash drawings were:",
 m(64300 + 350 - 41800 - 15000 - 500), [m(64300 - 41800 - 15000), m(64300 - 41800 - 15000 + 150), m(64300 + 350 - 41800 - 500)],
 "Cash available = $350 + $64,300 = $64,650. Less payments $41,800, bankings $15,000 and closing cash $500 leaves drawings of $7,350."),
("In a company's statement of financial position, a bank overdraft is normally presented as:",
 "A current liability", ["A deduction from cash", "A non-current liability", "A component of equity"],
 "An overdraft is repayable on demand, so it is a current liability. It is not offset against cash at other banks."),
("Which item must be presented as a line on the face of the statement of profit or loss?",
 "Income tax expense", ["Directors' salaries", "Each class of inventory", "Depreciation by asset class"],
 "Revenue and income tax expense are among the required line items. Details such as depreciation by class and inventory classes go in the notes."),
]
